I added `migrations/003_exports_status_default.sql`. I haven't run it or tested it against a database.

```sql
update exports set status = 'queued' where status is null;
alter table exports alter column status set default 'queued';
alter table exports alter column status set not null;
```

- **New migration:** I didn't edit `001_init.sql`, because it has probably already been applied wherever the table exists.
- **Backfill:** The first statement sets existing NULL rows to `'queued'`. Without it, `SET NOT NULL` would fail on those rows. If some of those jobs have really finished or failed, 'queued' will be wrong for them, so check before applying.
- **Order:** The `update` has to run before `SET NOT NULL`, so keep the statements in this order.

I didn't check `src/exports/sink.ts` for code that writes `status` explicitly. An explicit NULL insert would now be rejected.
